      "bounds": "Time Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ | Space Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(1)$",
      "mantra": "- Dynamic window $[L, R]$ expands while elements are $1$; encountering $0$ invalidates the streak.\n- Advance $R$ to increment running count; reset count to $0$ and snap $L = R + 1$ upon seeing $0$.\n- Maintain a global maximum across every step to handle terminal sequences of $1$s.",
      "leetcode": "https://leetcode.com/problems/max-consecutive-ones/",
      "tuf": "https://takeuforward.org/data-structure/count-maximum-consecutive-ones-in-the-array/",
      "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    // Function to find maximum consecutive 1's in an array\n    int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(vector<int> &nums) {\n        // Variable to store current count of consecutive 1's\n        int cnt = 0;\n        // Variable to store maximum consecutive 1's\n        int maxi = 0;\n\n        // Traverse the array\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {\n            // If current element is 1, increment count\n            if (nums[i] == 1) {\n                cnt++;\n            } else {\n                // If element is 0, reset count\n                cnt = 0;\n            }\n\n            // Update maximum if current count is greater\n            maxi = max(maxi, cnt);\n        }\n\n        // Return maximum consecutive 1's\n        return maxi;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    // Input array\n    vector<int> nums = {1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1};\n\n    // Create Solution object\n    Solution obj;\n\n    // Get answer\n    int ans = obj.findMaxConsecutiveOnes(nums);\n\n    // Print result\n    cout << \"The maximum consecutive 1's are \" << ans;\n    return 0;\n}",
      "py": "class Solution:\n    # Function to find maximum consecutive 1's in an array\n    def findMaxConsecutiveOnes(self, nums):\n        # Variable to store current count of consecutive 1's\n        cnt = 0\n        # Variable to store maximum consecutive 1's\n        maxi = 0\n\n        # Traverse the array\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\n            # If current element is 1, increment count\n            if nums[i] == 1:\n                cnt += 1\n            else:\n                # If element is 0, reset count\n                cnt = 0\n\n            # Update maximum if current count is greater\n            maxi = max(maxi, cnt)\n\n        # Return maximum consecutive 1's\n        return maxi\n\n# Input array\nnums = [1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1]\n\n# Create Solution object\nobj = Solution()\n\n# Get answer\nans = obj.findMaxConsecutiveOnes(nums)\n\n# Print result\nprint(\"The maximum consecutive 1's are\", ans)"
