      "title": "Allocate contiguous books to m students such that the maximum pages assigned to any student is minimized.",
      "canonicalName": "Allocate Minimum Number of Pages",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "bounds": "Time Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log(\\sum A))$ | Space Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(1)$",
      "mantra": "- Invariant Delta: Feasibility predicate $P(mid)$ is monotonic over answer space $[\\max(A), \\sum A]$.\n- Mechanics: Greedily aggregate book pages into student partitions; set $low = mid + 1$ if required students exceed $m$.\n- Edge/Trap: Return -1 immediately if the number of books is strictly less than $m$ students.",
      "leetcode": "",
      "tuf": "https://takeuforward.org/data-structure/allocate-minimum-number-of-pages/",
      "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution{\npublic:\n\nint countStudents(vector<int> &arr, int pages) {\n    int n = arr.size(); //size of array.\n    int students = 1;\n    long long pagesStudent = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (pagesStudent + arr[i] <= pages) {\n            //add pages to current student\n            pagesStudent += arr[i];\n        }\n        else {\n            //add pages to next student\n            students++;\n            pagesStudent = arr[i];\n        }\n    }\n    return students;\n}\n\nint findPages(vector<int>& arr, int n, int m) {\n    //book allocation impossible:\n    if (m > n) return -1;\n\n    int low = *max_element(arr.begin(), arr.end());\n    int high = accumulate(arr.begin(), arr.end(), 0);\n    while (low <= high) {\n        int mid = (low + high) / 2;\n        int students = countStudents(arr, mid);\n        if (students > m) {\n            low = mid + 1;\n        }\n        else {\n            high = mid - 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return low;\n}\n};\n\nint main()\n{\n    vector<int> arr = {25, 46, 28, 49, 24};\n    int n = 5;\n    int m = 4;\n    int ans = findPages(arr, n, m);\n    cout << \"The answer is: \" << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}",
      "py": "def countStudents(arr, pages):\n    n = len(arr)  # size of array\n    students = 1\n    pagesStudent = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        if pagesStudent + arr[i] <= pages:\n            # add pages to current student\n            pagesStudent += arr[i]\n        else:\n            # add pages to next student\n            students += 1\n            pagesStudent = arr[i]\n    return students\n\ndef findPages(arr, n, m):\n    # book allocation impossible\n    if m > n:\n        return -1\n\n    low = max(arr)\n    high = sum(arr)\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        students = countStudents(arr, mid)\n        if students > m:\n            low = mid + 1  # Trim down the left part of the array\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1  # Trim down the right part of the array\n    return low\n\narr = [25, 46, 28, 49, 24]\nn = 5\nm = 4\nans = findPages(arr, n, m)\nprint(\"The answer is:\", ans)"
