      "patternName": "In Place Mutation and Pointer Rewiring",
      "problemSeq": 6,
      "title": "Rotate an $N \\times N$ 2D matrix by 90 degrees clockwise in-place.",
      "canonicalName": "Rotate matrix by 90 degrees",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "bounds": "Time Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ | Space Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(1)$",
      "mantra": "- Invariant Delta: Decompose spatial rotation into coordinate transpose followed by horizontal row reversal.\n- Mechanics: Swap `matrix[r][c]` with `matrix[c][r]` for $c > r$; reverse elements along each horizontal vector.\n- Edge/Trap: Restrict transpose loop to $c > r$; transposing the entire matrix double-swaps cells back.",
      "leetcode": "https://leetcode.com/problems/rotate-image/",
      "tuf": "https://takeuforward.org/data-structure/rotate-image-by-90-degree/",
      "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    // Function to rotate matrix 90 degrees clockwise in-place\n    void rotateClockwise(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {\n        int n = matrix.size();\n\n        // Step 1: Transpose the matrix\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; ++j) {\n                // Swap element at (i, j) with (j, i) to transpose\n                swap(matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Step 2: Reverse each row\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            // Reverse the current row to complete clockwise rotation\n            reverse(matrix[i].begin(), matrix[i].end());\n        }\n    }\n};\n\n// Driver code\nint main() {\n    vector<vector<int>> matrix = {\n        {1, 2, 3},\n        {4, 5, 6},\n        {7, 8, 9}\n    };\n\n    Solution obj;\n    obj.rotateClockwise(matrix);\n\n    // Print rotated matrix\n    for (auto row : matrix) {\n        for (int val : row) {\n            cout << val << \" \";\n        }\n        cout << endl;\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}",
      "py": "class Solution:\n    # Function to rotate matrix 90 degrees clockwise in-place\n    def rotateClockwise(self, matrix):\n        n = len(matrix)\n\n        # Step 1: Transpose the matrix\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                # Swap element at (i, j) with (j, i)\n                matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i] = matrix[j][i], matrix[i][j]\n\n        # Step 2: Reverse each row\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Reverse the current row to simulate clockwise rotation\n            matrix[i].reverse()\n\n# Driver code\nmatrix = [\n    [1, 2, 3],\n    [4, 5, 6],\n    [7, 8, 9]\n]\n\nobj = Solution()\nobj.rotateClockwise(matrix)\n\n# Print rotated matrix\nfor row in matrix:\n    print(*row)"
