      "title": "Find the minimum number of coins needed to make up a target amount using canonical currency denominations.",
      "canonicalName": "Minimum coins",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "bounds": "Time Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ | Space Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(1)$",
      "mantra": "- Invariant Delta: Greedily subtract the largest denomination $c_i \\le \\text{remaining\\_amount}$.\n- Mechanics: Iterate denominations in descending order; take $\\lfloor \\text{amount} / c_i \\rfloor$ coins, update amount with modulo.\n- Edge/Trap: Canonical currency systems guarantee greedy optimality; arbitrary denominations fail and require DP.",
      "leetcode": "https://leetcode.com/problems/coin-change/",
      "tuf": "https://takeuforward.org/data-structure/minimum-coins-dp-20/",
      "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\n// Solution class to implement tabulation approach\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    // Function to find minimum coins\n    int coinChange(vector<int>& coins, int amount) {\n        // Creating dp array of size amount+1\n        vector<int> dp(amount + 1, INT_MAX);\n\n        // Base case: dp[0] = 0\n        dp[0] = 0;\n\n        // Loop through all amounts from 1 to amount\n        for (int i = 1; i <= amount; i++) {\n            // Try each coin\n            for (int coin : coins) {\n                // If coin can be used\n                if (i - coin >= 0 && dp[i - coin] != INT_MAX) {\n                    // Update dp[i] with minimum coins\n                    dp[i] = min(dp[i], 1 + dp[i - coin]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // If dp[amount] is still infinity, return -1\n        return dp[amount] == INT_MAX ? -1 : dp[amount];\n    }\n};\n\n// Driver function\nint main() {\n    vector<int> coins = {1, 2, 5};\n    int amount = 11;\n\n    Solution obj;\n    cout << obj.coinChange(coins, amount) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}",
      "py": "# Solution class to implement tabulation approach\nclass Solution:\n    # Function to find minimum coins\n    def coinChange(self, coins, amount):\n        # Creating dp array of size amount+1\n        dp = [float('inf')] * (amount + 1)\n\n        # Base case: dp[0] = 0\n        dp[0] = 0\n\n        # Loop through all amounts from 1 to amount\n        for i in range(1, amount + 1):\n            # Try each coin\n            for coin in coins:\n                # If coin can be used\n                if i - coin >= 0 and dp[i - coin] != float('inf'):\n                    # Update dp[i] with minimum coins\n                    dp[i] = min(dp[i], 1 + dp[i - coin])\n\n        # If dp[amount] is still infinity, return -1\n        return -1 if dp[amount] == float('inf') else dp[amount]\n\n\n# Driver function\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    coins = [1, 2, 5]\n    amount = 11\n\n    obj = Solution()\n    print(obj.coinChange(coins, amount))"
