      "patternName": "Greedy Selection and Interval Scheduling",
      "problemSeq": 6,
      "title": "Find the minimum number of railway platforms required so that no arriving train is delayed.",
      "canonicalName": "Minimum number of platforms required for a railway",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "bounds": "Time Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ | Space Complexity: $\\mathcal{O}(1)$",
      "mantra": "- Invariant Delta: Chronological sweep-line across decoupled arrival and departure events.\n- Mechanics: Sort arrivals and departures independently; increment count on arrival, decrement on departure, track peak count.\n- Edge/Trap: Simultaneous arrival and departure ($arr[i] == dep[j]$); arrival must be prioritized to prevent undercounting.",
      "leetcode": "",
      "tuf": "https://takeuforward.org/data-structure/minimum-number-of-platforms-required-for-a-railway/",
      "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass Solution {\npublic:\n    // Function to find minimum platforms required\n    int countPlatforms(int n, int arr[], int dep[]) {\n        // Sort the arrival and departure times\n        sort(arr, arr + n);\n        sort(dep, dep + n);\n\n        // Initialize pointers and counters\n        int platforms = 1;\n        int result = 1;\n        int i = 1, j = 0;\n\n        // Traverse both arrays\n        while (i < n && j < n) {\n            // If next train arrives before current one departs\n            if (arr[i] <= dep[j]) {\n                // One more platform needed\n                platforms++;\n                i++;\n            } else {\n                // One train departs, platform freed\n                platforms--;\n                j++;\n            }\n\n            // Update maximum required platforms\n            result = max(result, platforms);\n        }\n\n        return result;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int arr[] = {900, 945, 955, 1100, 1500, 1800};\n    int dep[] = {920, 1200, 1130, 1150, 1900, 2000};\n    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);\n\n    Solution obj;\n    cout << \"Minimum number of Platforms required \" \n         << obj.countPlatforms(n, arr, dep) << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}",
      "py": "class Solution:\n    def countPlatforms(self, arr, dep, n):\n        # Sort both lists\n        arr.sort()\n        dep.sort()\n\n        # Initialize pointers and counters\n        platforms = 1\n        result = 1\n        i, j = 1, 0\n\n        # Traverse arrival and departure\n        while i < n and j < n:\n            # If train arrives before previous departs\n            if arr[i] <= dep[j]:\n                platforms += 1\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                platforms -= 1\n                j += 1\n\n            # Update max platform count\n            result = max(result, platforms)\n\n        return result\n\n# Driver code\narr = [900, 945, 955, 1100, 1500, 1800]\ndep = [920, 1200, 1130, 1150, 1900, 2000]\nn = len(arr)\n\nobj = Solution()\nprint(\"Minimum number of Platforms required\",\n      obj.countPlatforms(arr, dep, n))"
